    "created_at": "2016-07-13T23:27:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-13T23:27:25Z",
    "body": "Current state of affairs, according to the test case in https://bug1273068.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=8752835:\n\n| Browser | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Firefox 49 | non-:hover color: clipped bg color. on-:hover: -webkit-text-color is displayed and animated, clipped bg text color displayed when :hover animation ends. |\n| Chrome 54 | non-:hover color: clipped bg color. on-:hover: \"ghosted\" (👻) -webkit-text-color is displayed and animated, but clipped bg color remains in place. clipped bg text color displayed when :hover animation ends. |\n| Safari Tech Preview Release 8 | non-:hover color: -webkit-text-color. on-:hover: -webkit-text-color is displayed and animated. -webkit-text-color displayed when :hover animation ends |\n| Edge 38.14342.something | matches Safari Tech Preview |\n\nThat Safari displays -webkit-text-color for the non-hover case is likely just a bug -- if you inspect the element in devtools, you can get -webkit-background-clip: text to work as expected (after the hover animation ends).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
